From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fritchii_write_ring: strncpy bound leaves room for NUL

GCC 13 on ubuntu-24.04-arm with -Werror=stringop-truncation rejects
strncpy(..., 16) into a 16-byte buffer. Size-1 matches the intent (16-char
name storage that is memcpy'd as raw bytes).

---
 src/common/fritchii_write_ring.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/fritchii_write_ring.h b/src/common/fritchii_write_ring.h
--- a/src/common/fritchii_write_ring.h
+++ b/src/common/fritchii_write_ring.h
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ inline thread_local bool t_quiet = false;
 inline void NameThread(const char* name) noexcept {
     std::array<char, 16> chars{};
     if (name != nullptr) {
-        std::strncpy(chars.data(), name, chars.size());
+        std::strncpy(chars.data(), name, chars.size() - 1);
     }
     std::memcpy(t_thread.data(), chars.data(), chars.size());
 }
